# AtomVM-unsafe Gleam / OTP stdlib

Host `gleam test` (OTP) can pass while the **badge** crashes. Prefer APIs that operate on
binaries/`BitArray` and plain list cons. When the monitor shows
`cannot be resolved` or `badarg` in `lists:reverse` / `string:*`, check this list.

## Never use on badge code

| Avoid | Why | Symptom |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `string.lowercase` / `string.uppercase` | No AtomVM `string:lowercase/1` (etc.) | `cannot be resolved` → often `undef` |
| `string.trim` / `string.trim_start` / `string.trim_end` | Grapheme path → `lists:reverse` on a UTF-8 binary | `badarg` in `lists:reverse` |
| `string.slice` / `string.drop_*` / grapheme iterators for edits | Same grapheme / list assumption | `badarg` or wrong results |
| Growing with `list.append(xs, [one])` | Prefer cons; append is easy to get wrong under memory pressure | Prefer prepend |

`string.length` / `<>` / `<<text:utf8>>` are usually fine for ASCII labels.

## Replacements

### Case fold (letters)

```gleam
// ❌ BAD
Some(chat.Type(string.lowercase(name)))

// ✅ GOOD — store the label already cased (see 12_tea keymap)
Some("q")  // in the layout table
Some(chat.Type(name))
```

Or a tiny ASCII table if you must convert at runtime:

```gleam
fn ascii_lower(ch: String) -> String {
  case ch {
    "A" -> "a"
    "B" -> "b"
    // …
    _ -> ch
  }
}
```

### Trim / empty draft

```gleam
// ❌ BAD
case string.trim(model.draft) {
  "" -> model
  body -> …
}

// ✅ GOOD — exact empty (or strip spaces yourself with bit_array)
case model.draft {
  "" -> model
  body -> …
}
```

### Drop last character (ASCII / single-byte)

```gleam
// ❌ BAD
string.slice(text, 0, string.length(text) - 1)

// ✅ GOOD
fn drop_last(text: String) -> String {
  let bits = <<text:utf8>>
  let n = bit_array.byte_size(bits)
  case n {
    0 -> ""
    _ ->
      case bit_array.slice(bits, 0, n - 1) {
        Ok(prefix) ->
          case bit_array.to_string(prefix) {
            Ok(s) -> s
            Error(Nil) -> text
          }
        Error(Nil) -> text
      }
  }
}
```

### Grow a message / event list

```gleam
// ❌ BAD
messages: list.append(model.messages, [Line("You", body)])

// ✅ GOOD — newest first; reverse when painting oldest-at-top
messages: [Line("You", body), ..model.messages]
```

